@node MAIN
@next START

@{c}@{h1}NexBrowse

@{c}A text web browser for the ZX Spectrum Next

NexBrowse shows web pages as text, with highlighted links that you can
follow. A NexBrowse server on the internet fetches each page and turns it
into a few kilobytes of plain text that the Next can display quickly.

 @{" Starting NexBrowse " LINK START}
 @{" The screen " LINK SCREEN}
 @{" Keys when reading a page " LINK KEYS_PAGE}
 @{" Keys in the address field " LINK KEYS_URL}
 @{" Typing symbols in addresses " LINK SYMBOLS}
 @{" Links and long pages " LINK LINKS}
 @{" Pictures " LINK PICTURES}
 @{" Settings: NEXBROWSE.CFG " LINK CONFIG}
 @{" Messages on the status line " LINK MESSAGES}
 @{" What NexBrowse cannot do " LINK LIMITS}
 @{" Quick key reference " LINK QUICKREF}

@{h2}Reading this guide

@{i}Right@{ui}/@{i}Left@{ui} select a link, @{i}ENTER@{ui} follows it, @{i}B@{ui} goes back.
@{i}N@{ui} and @{i}P@{ui} turn the pages, @{i}C@{ui} returns to the contents, @{i}Q@{ui} quits.

@-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@node START
@next SCREEN
@prev MAIN
@toc MAIN
@{r}NexBrowse Guide
@{c}@{h1}Starting NexBrowse

@{h2}Before the first use

1) The Next's Wi-Fi module must have joined your network once. Use the
   NextZXOS Wi-Fi setup program. The module remembers the network.
2) NexBrowse.nex and NEXBROWSE.CFG must be in the same folder on the SD
   card, and NEXBROWSE.CFG must name your NexBrowse server
   (see @{" Settings " LINK CONFIG}).

@{h2}Running it

Open the NextZXOS @{b}Browser@{ub}, go to the folder, select @{b}NexBrowse.nex@{ub}
and press @{i}ENTER@{ui}. From NextBASIC you can also type:

    @{b}.nexload nexbrowse.nex@{ub}

The welcome screen shows the server (only its first 5 letters; the rest
appear as *) and whether NEXBROWSE.CFG was read.

The address field already holds your home page. Press @{i}ENTER@{ui} to open
it, or type another address first. The first page takes a little longer
because NexBrowse checks the Wi-Fi module.

@-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@node SCREEN
@next KEYS_PAGE
@prev START
@toc MAIN
@{r}NexBrowse Guide
@{c}@{h1}The screen

From top to bottom:

 @{b}Address bar@{ub}   " URL " then the address field. Type an address
               and press ENTER to open it. On the right, the
               [ ] Images box: press I to tick it (see Pictures).
 @{b}Title bar@{ub}     The page title. "Page 2/7" on the right means you are
               reading section 2 of 7 of a long page.
 @{b}Page text@{ub}     Headings in yellow, text in white, links in purple.
               The selected link is shown in reverse.
               @{b}[ Next Page ]@{ub} appears after the last line when the page
               has more sections.
 @{b}Help line@{ub}     The keys you can use right now.
 @{b}Status line@{ub}   What NexBrowse is doing, or what went wrong (errors
               appear in red).

One thing has @{i}focus@{ui} at a time: the address field or the page. The focused one is highlighted, and the help line changes with it.
@{i}EXTEND MODE@{ui} moves the focus, but you rarely need it: @{i}U@{ui} jumps to
the address field and @{i}ENTER@{ui} or a cursor key goes back to the page.

@-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@node KEYS_PAGE
@next KEYS_URL
@prev SCREEN
@toc MAIN
@{r}NexBrowse Guide
@{c}@{h1}Keys when reading a page

@{i}Key                 What it does@{ui}

Cursor Down/Right   Choose the next link
Cursor Up/Left      Choose the previous link
ENTER               Open the chosen link (or [ Next Page ])
SPACE               Scroll down one screen
DELETE              Scroll up one screen
N                   Next page of a long article
B                   Back to where you were before
R                   Reload
H                   Home page
U                   Type a new address
I                   Pictures on/off
Q                   Quit (then Y to confirm)

That is all you need. Links are chosen in reading order; if the next link
is a long way down, the cursor key scrolls the text instead so you never
skip over anything. The status line shows where the chosen link leads.

These keys work the same way as in this guide viewer.

@{h2}Extra keys

EXTEND MODE        Switch between the page and the address field
EDIT               Un-choose the highlighted link
INV/TRUE VIDEO     Also scroll down / up one screen
@-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@node KEYS_URL
@next SYMBOLS
@prev KEYS_PAGE
@toc MAIN
@{r}NexBrowse Guide
@{c}@{h1}Keys in the address field

@{i}Key                 What it does@{ui}

letters, numbers    Type (hold CAPS SHIFT for capitals)
SYMBOL SHIFT + key  Type a symbol such as : / . ?  - see @{" Symbols " LINK SYMBOLS}
Cursor Left/Right   Move the cursor
DELETE              Rub out the character before the cursor
GRAPH               Clear the whole field
ENTER               Go to the address
EDIT                Cancel: put back the page's address and return
                    to the page
Cursor Up/Down      Go back to the page

@{h2}Addresses

You can leave out the @{i}https://@{ui} part: @{b}en.wikipedia.org@{ub} works.
Spaces are not allowed in an address.
@-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@node SYMBOLS
@next LINKS
@prev KEYS_URL
@toc MAIN
@{r}NexBrowse Guide
@{c}@{h1}Typing symbols in addresses

Hold SYMBOL SHIFT and press the key:

@{i}Symbol  Key        Symbol  Key        Symbol  Key@{ui}
  :      Z            /      V            .      M
  ?      C            =      L            &      6
  -      J            +      K            _      0
  %      5            #      3            ~      A
  @@      2            ,      N            *      B
  ;      O            "      P            '      7
  !      1            $      4            (  )   8  9
  [      Y            ]      U            <  >   R  T
  |      S            \      D            {  }   F  G
  ^      H            `      X

Example: @{b}en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ZX_Spectrum@{ub} is typed with
SYMBOL SHIFT + M for each full stop, SYMBOL SHIFT + V for each slash and
SYMBOL SHIFT + 0 for the underscore.

@-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@node LINKS
@next PICTURES
@prev SYMBOLS
@toc MAIN
@{r}NexBrowse Guide
@{c}@{h1}Links and long pages

@{h2}Following links

Press Down to select the first link, keep pressing to move through the
links, then press ENTER. The new page replaces the current one, and B
brings the old one back.

@{h2}Long pages

The server cuts long pages into sections of about 2000 characters, so the
first part appears quickly. "Page 1/12" in the title bar means there are
12 sections. To read on, press @{b}N@{ub}, or select @{b}[ Next Page ]@{ub} at
the end of the text and press ENTER. B steps back a section at a time.

Within a section, SPACE scrolls down a screen and DELETE scrolls back up.

@{h2}History

B remembers the last 6 pages, including which section you were reading.

@{h2}Expired pages

The server keeps pages for a while (up to an hour). If you come back after
that, NexBrowse fetches the page again by itself and carries on.

@-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@node PICTURES
@next CONFIG
@prev LINKS
@toc MAIN
@{r}NexBrowse Guide
@{c}@{h1}Pictures

NexBrowse can show small pictures from a page. They are off at first, so
pages load as fast as possible.

Press @{b}I@{ub} on a page to tick the box at the top right:

    @{b}[X] Images@{ub}

The text appears first, as usual, with a line such as
@{b}[Image] Rainbow test card@{ub} where each picture goes. Then the pictures
arrive one by one and the text moves down to make room for them. You can
keep reading and pressing keys while they load.

Press @{b}I@{ub} again to hide the pictures.

@{h2}What to expect

Pictures are small (at most about 160 by 120 dots) and use 16 colours, so
they are a rough preview. Each section of a page shows at most 2 pictures.
Icons, logos drawn as SVG, and pictures added by JavaScript are not shown.

If a picture cannot be fetched you see @{b}[Image not available]@{ub} and its
description instead. The text is not affected.

To have the box ticked every time NexBrowse starts, put @{b}images=1@{ub} in
NEXBROWSE.CFG.

@-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@node CONFIG
@next MESSAGES
@prev PICTURES
@toc MAIN
@{r}NexBrowse Guide
@{c}@{h1}Settings: NEXBROWSE.CFG

NEXBROWSE.CFG is a text file in the same folder as NexBrowse.nex. Each line
is @{b}name=value@{ub}; lines starting with # are ignored. Any line can be left
out to use the built-in default.

@{i}Setting          Meaning@{ui}
server=          Your NexBrowse server's name, for example
                 myserver.azurewebsites.net (host:port also works)
port=            Server port, normally 80
key=             Access key, if your server needs one
home=            The page opened at start-up
text_colour=     Colour of page text          (default white)
link_colour=     Colour of links              (default purple)
screen_rows=     Rows used on screen, 22 to 32 (default 24)
images=          1 = pictures on at start-up   (default 0)
tls=             Leave at 0 (experimental)

@{h2}Colours

Use a name: white black grey lightgrey red green blue yellow cyan magenta
purple orange pink lightblue lightgreen brown. Or give a Next colour number
(RRRGGGBB) such as 171, 0xAB, $AB or #AB.

@{h2}screen_rows

24 uses the normal Spectrum screen area, which every TV and monitor shows.
If your display shows more of the border, try 26, 28 or even 32 to see more
text at once. If the top or bottom gets cut off, use a lower number.

@-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@node MESSAGES
@next LIMITS
@prev CONFIG
@toc MAIN
@{r}NexBrowse Guide
@{c}@{h1}Messages on the status line

@{b}Wi-Fi module not responding@{ub}
  The Wi-Fi module did not answer. Check it is fitted; try .uart and AT.
@{b}Wi-Fi not connected - run the NextZXOS Wi-Fi setup@{ub}
  The module has not joined a network. Run the Wi-Fi setup once.
@{b}Connection failed (server unreachable or DNS)@{ub}
  Check server= and port= in NEXBROWSE.CFG, and that the server is running.
@{b}Connection failed: Connection timed out@{ub}
  Weak Wi-Fi, or the server was asleep. Press R to try again.
@{b}Error: Access key missing or wrong@{ub}
  key= in NEXBROWSE.CFG does not match the server.
@{b}Error: Destination is not allowed@{ub}
  The server refuses local and private addresses. This is normal.
@{b}Error: Site returned HTTP 404@{ub} (or another number)
  The website itself reported an error.
@{b}Error: Not a web page@{ub}
  The link leads to an image, PDF or download. Only text is shown.
@{b}Invalid URL@{ub}
  The address contains a space or does not look like an address.
@{b}Page loaded, but the response was incomplete@{ub}
  The connection dropped. Press R.
@{b}Page expired on the server - reloading...@{ub}
  Normal after a long pause; NexBrowse fetches the page again.
@{b}Image not available@{ub}
  A picture could not be fetched or is not a supported kind. Only that
  picture is missing; the text is fine.
@{b}Not enough free memory for images@{ub}
  NextZXOS had no spare memory for pictures. Text browsing still works.

After any error the page you were reading stays on screen, and the address
you typed is kept so you can correct it. B and R still work.

@-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@node LIMITS
@next QUICKREF
@prev MESSAGES
@toc MAIN
@{r}NexBrowse Guide
@{c}@{h1}What NexBrowse cannot do

@{b}No JavaScript.@{ub} Pages that build their text with JavaScript, and some
"checking your browser" pages, show little or nothing.

@{b}No forms, logins or downloads.@{ub} Text, links and small pictures are
shown. To search, type the search address directly, for example
en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=sinclair

@{b}Plain letters only.@{ub} Accents are removed (an accented e shows as a
plain e) and other alphabets, such as Japanese or Cyrillic, cannot be shown.

@{b}Not private.@{ub} The connection between the Next and the NexBrowse server
is not encrypted, so do not use NexBrowse for anything confidential.

@{b}Menus are moved to the end.@{ub} The server shows the main text of a page
first. Anything that looks like a long menu (a list of short links, or a
bar of links) appears after the text, under "Menus" or "Site navigation".
If a page is mostly links, it is left as it is.

@-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@node QUICKREF
@prev LIMITS
@toc MAIN
@{r}NexBrowse Guide
@{c}@{h1}Quick key reference

@{h2}Reading a page
 Cursor keys   choose a link        ENTER    open it
 SPACE         scroll down          DELETE   scroll up
 N   next page      B   back        R   reload
 H   home           U   new address Q   quit
 I   pictures on/off

@{h2}Typing an address
 SYMBOL SHIFT + Z :   V /   M .   C ?   L =   J -   0 _
 Cursor Left/Right   move     DELETE   rub out     GRAPH   clear
 ENTER   go                   EDIT     cancel
